---
import { icon } from '../../lib/icons.js';
---

<section id="conclusion" class="section" aria-labelledby="conclusion-title">
  <div class="section-inner">
    <h2 id="conclusion-title">04 Conclusions</h2>
    <aside class="takeaway">
      <p>
        <span>Direct control</span>The two sides are complementary: the direct-control agent is
        stronger in{' '}
        <strong>
          visual grounding, robustness across generalization dimensions, in-episode adaptation, and
          zero-shot skill composition
        </strong>
        , and the post-trained policies in <strong>closed-loop physical execution</strong>.
      </p>
    </aside>
    <aside class="takeaway">
      <p>
        <span>Harness with policy</span>With a post-trained policy, the agent reaches further on{' '}
        <strong>long-horizon and tabletop tasks at a lower token cost per success</strong>, but it
        remains bounded by{' '}
        <strong>high-precision contact, which none of its components masters</strong>, and by{' '}
        <strong>loose coordination in delegation, subgoals, and control transfer</strong>.
      </p>
    </aside>
    <div class="report-prose">
      <h3>Future directions</h3>
      <ol class="direction-list">
        <li>Designing subtask interfaces and training policies as learnable tools</li>
        <li>Grounding exploratory experience into reusable memory and tools</li>
        <li>Transferring the agent's exploratory and corrective strategies to smaller policies</li>
        <li>Coupling geometric perception with active safety constraints in execution</li>
      </ol>
      <p>
        <a
          class="paper-link"
          href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.35832"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener"
        >
          Read the full report on arXiv <Fragment set:html={icon('external-link')} />
        </a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
